<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick I of Prussia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1657–1713</span> · Also known as Frederick III, Elector of Brandenburg, Frederick III of Brandenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> succeeded as Elector Frederick III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in 1688. In 1701, with the emperor's consent, he crowned himself King in Prussia at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>, raising the status of the Hohenzollern lands. A patron of the arts and learning, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prussian-academy-of-sciences">Prussian Academy of Sciences</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-halle">University of Halle</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-prussia.jpg" alt="Frederick I of Prussia" width="320" height="577" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Wilhelm Weidemann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frederick_I_of_Prussia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
